### Handling the Score

Since `Document` doesn’t store the score natively:
- **Metadata Approach**: As shown, store it in `metadata` under `"similarityScore"`. Access it via `doc.getMetadata().get("similarityScore")`.
- **Custom Wrapper**: If you need the score more explicitly, create a wrapper class:
  ```java
  public class ScoredDocument {
      private final Document document;
      private final double score;

      public ScoredDocument(Document document, double score) {
          this.document = document;
          this.score = score;
      }

      public Document getDocument() { return document; }
      public double getScore() { return score; }
  }

  public List<ScoredDocument> retrieve(String query) {
      // ... same aggregation logic ...
      return results.stream()
              .filter(result -> (double) result.get("score") >= 0.7)
              .map(result -> new ScoredDocument(
                      new Document((String) result.get("content"), (Map<String, Object>) result.get("metadata")),
                      (double) result.get("score")
              ))
              .collect(Collectors.toList());
  }
  ```

